#: ../../source/user-guide/rerope/rerope.md:15
msgid "🌟 What is ReRoPE?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/rerope/rerope.md:23
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This approach combines direct extrapolation with position interpolation. "
"A window size $w$ is established, where a position interval of $1$ is "
"used within the window, and an interval of $\\frac{1}{k}$ is applied "
"outside. As $k \\to \\infty$, this simplifies to the form illustrated "
"above. Under this scheme, the position encoding range never exceeds $w$ "
"regardless of input length, potentially enabling support for arbitrarily "
"long contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/rerope/rerope.md:25
msgid "The attention score calculation formulas are as follows,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/rerope/rerope.md:27
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"$$ \\begin{aligned} score_{ij}^{1} &= (q_iR_i)(k_jR_j)^T, && i-j<w \\\\ "
"score_{ij}^{2} &= (q_iR_w)(k_j)^T, && i-j\\ge w \\end{aligned} $$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/rerope/rerope.md:34
msgid ""
"ReRoPE extends context length effectively but requires double "
"attention—local within w and global compressed—significantly reducing "
"throughput. Despite this overhead, it remains valuable for training-free "
"long contexts, especially when combined with local attention windows to "
"balance efficiency."
msgstr ""

